---
description: Stash-and-restart sequence to use when the current branch's PR already merged into main
alwaysApply: false
---

# Recover from a merged branch

**Precondition:** no merge or rebase in progress. If one exists, stop and ask the user.

1. Confirm: `gh pr list --state merged --head <current-branch> --json number,mergedAt,mergeCommit`.
2. `git stash -u`
3. Fast-forward `main` without checking it out: `git fetch . origin/main:main`
   (on `main` already: `git merge --ff-only origin/main`).
4. `git checkout -b <new-branch-name> main`
5. `git stash apply` (not `pop`), verify what is still needed, then `git stash drop`.
